<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><subtitle type="html">Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/rss</id><updated>2026-11-03T21:52:29Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>South Africa braces for some job losses as AGOA ends</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:026705df6c39b9a8ecdf1bbcc4b6220e6d7ee69e81e7e473a769495b2db83875</id><updated>2026-11-03T21:52:29Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T21:18:25Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/south-africa-braces-for-some-job-losses-as-agoa-ends" /><summary type="html">In tonight's edition, Rwanda and South Africa will lose their duty-free access to the U.S. market after being excluded from the AGOA trade program. Also, South Africans head to the polls amid water shortages and frustration with local services. And  in the DRC's mining capital, Kolwezi, residents are taking on one of the country's largest Chinese-owned mines... accusing it of poisoning their environment.</summary><category term="Eye on Africa" /></entry><entry><title>Trump promised a 'Golden Age'. What has he delivered at home?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a185518a9fa7a1f5ceb6acd3cba69064da3e7b727c48e29a63033b69e2d96635</id><updated>2026-11-03T21:52:29Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T20:56:49Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/truth-or-fake/20261103-trump-promised-a-golden-age-what-has-he-delivered-at-home" /><summary type="html">Donald Trump promised Americans a “Golden Age” when he returned to the White House in January 2025. Since then, his administration has slashed government spending through DOGE, ramped up mass deportations, expanded ICE operations and pursued an aggressive crackdown on DEI programmes and transgender rights. But how much has he actually achieved, and at what cost? Vedika Bahl examines Trump's domestic agenda since returning to office.</summary><category term="Truth or Fake" /></entry><entry><title>Trickle or tsunami? Democrats eye gains in US midterm elections</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d9d7d4f2bd833e08385026c0c0e8d980de10212c1d546a79c5cd89051dc36228</id><updated>2026-11-03T21:52:29Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T19:18:13Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20261103-trickle-or-tsunami-democrats-eye-gains-in-us-midterm-elections" /><summary type="html">Will it be a trickle, a wave, or a tsunami? Election Day in the United States with Democrats hoping to take back one or both houses of Congress. We’ll track the turnout, gauge the mood and raise the curtain ahead of Midterms results that are sure to shape the last two years of Donald Trump’s second and final term. Will a US president who’s already broken norms with his maximum use of executive powers be affected by the results a little, a lot, or not at all?</summary><category term="The Debate" /></entry><entry><title>🔴 Midterms live: Voting under way to determine control of Congress and the future of Trump's agenda</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b0866900273ca166618aebb9bb6263c5086144fa8c72ebd55ff1dc0aefd60257</id><updated>2026-11-03T21:52:29Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T18:42:49Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261103-live-americans-head-to-the-polls-to-vote-in-us-midterm-elections--73179ea277e3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261103-live-americans-head-to-the-polls-to-vote-in-us-midterm-elections" /></entry><entry><title>France's dermatology crisis: Patients desperate for appointments</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:02751e826d8ebb1596e48c050380482f470e6f1767b4ba51e3893ace35727e7e</id><updated>2026-11-03T21:52:29Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T17:34:50Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/france-in-focus/20261103-france-s-dermatology-crisis-patients-desperate-for-appointments" /><summary type="html">Around 200,000 cases of skin cancer are diagnosed in France every year. Yet as more and more patients seek medical advice, getting an appointment with a dermatologist is becoming increasingly difficult. Half the country's dermatologists are nearing retirement, and only around 100 new specialists are trained up each year. Faced with this growing shortage, some are coming up with innovative solutions. FRANCE 24's Aurore Dupuis and Sonia Baritello report.</summary><category term="France in focus" /></entry><entry><title>Family wealth, Epstein, ‘vanity projects’: How Democrats plan to investigate Trump after midterms</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c631dad35d423c18a8a625eacf207c5c415e12b6a10d53f61f9d6dc8f42c9b84</id><updated>2026-11-03T21:52:29Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T17:30:16Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261103-trump-family-wealth-epstein-vanity-projects-democrats-plan-to-investigate-after-midterms" /><summary type="html">Democrats are preparing to launch a flurry of investigations into President Donald Trump’s administration and business dealings if they retake one or both chambers of Congress, devising strategies to circumvent obstruction from the White House and avoid the impeachment deadlock that consumed the US legislature during Trump’s first term in office.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Russian households face increasing financial strain as war in Ukraine drags on</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:86c6b123675d6f31003f6c94686e7e3f1345f1c546928b1610d15e524a593b0e</id><updated>2026-11-03T21:52:29Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T17:05:54Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261103-russian-households-face-increasing-financial-strain-as-war-in-ukraine-drags-on" /><summary type="html">As Moscow continues to launch strikes across Ukraine, Russian citizens are facing increasing financial strain. Since the start of the war in 2022, utility bills in Russia have risen by more than 50% – over 13% this year alone. These rising costs come as the country grapples with ongoing drone attacks originating from Ukraine.</summary></entry><entry><title>Ukraine and Russia are taking the war underground as drones saturate the battlefield</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ee7de5ed316ed8c1f437441ac0a490e7568f349e73b894e62f8d291685319346</id><updated>2026-11-03T21:52:29Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T16:52:13Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261103-ukraine-and-russia-are-taking-the-war-underground-as-drones-saturate-the-battlefield" /><summary type="html">Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky last week heralded the success of Operation Veles, during which Kyiv sent troops deep into a disused gas pipeline in the Kupiansk region to confront Russian troops. These underground tactics, which Russian forces have been using for more than two years to slip past Ukrainian lines, are giving Kyiv a new strategy on the battlefield.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>US Midterms: Texas Democrat Talarico holds last rally ahead of vote</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:02123268aac409e55e31c73b8f5a4ed60737be721ccab6809920202f794106e5</id><updated>2026-11-03T21:52:29Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T16:50:55Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261103-us-midterms-texas-democrat-talarico-holds-last-rally-ahead-of-vote" /><summary type="html">Texas Democratic nominee James Talarico held a final rally Monday ahead of US midterm elections on November 3. His race against Republican Ken Paxton could determine which party holds a majority in the Senate. If Talarico wins, it will be the first time a Texas Senate seat's turned blue since 1988.</summary></entry><entry><title>US midterm elections: Over 58 million Americans cast early ballots</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:70233a856172c29d0bff7d42f274ed279987000a31154a12e01f2644bd9d980c</id><updated>2026-11-03T21:52:29Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T16:46:29Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261103-us-midterm-elections-over-58-million-americans-cast-early-ballots" /><summary type="html">How powerful is US President Donald Trump? That’s the question pollsters have been asking in the lead-up to the midterm elections. Polls have opened in dozens of US states in what is widely considered a referendum on Donald Trump. Most polls suggest Democrats will take back the House of Representatives, but could they also take the Senate and stymie Trump’s agenda during his final two years in office?</summary></entry><entry><title>US midterms: Talarico seeks to break Democrats' 30-year losing streak in Texas</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8c71c1dda76cf0f9d59f3a27827deb7c514aec1e8c2275221b4a0fd7b2f154be</id><updated>2026-11-03T21:52:29Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T16:45:33Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261103-us-midterms-talarico-seeks-to-break-democrats-30-year-losing-streak-in-texas" /><summary type="html">In Texas, Democratic candidate James Talarico is leading the polls ahead of a high-stakes US Senate race against Republican Ken Paxton. The contest is one of the most closely watched battles of the midterm elections, with Democrats hoping to end a 30-year losing streak in the state. FRANCE 24's Andrés Espinal reports from Austin, Texas.</summary></entry><entry><title>Election officials brace for possible Trump interference in the midterms</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7a2b8dc3e94321e6c3047e99116484d041bfed5f02525587b0e5efa128ddcf6d</id><updated>2026-11-03T21:52:29Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T16:41:47Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261103-how-state-officials-prepared-for-possible-trump-interference-in-the-midterms" /><summary type="html">State officials who run US elections braced for possible intervention by President Donald Trump's administration in Tuesday's midterms, fearing federal authorities loyal to the president could disrupt voting, challenge ballot counts or try to block the certification of unfavorable results.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Brazil keeps a close eye on US midterm elections</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bb2ccb7df000cdfd78417fcde0943c600d4c23dd0dd941ae5e6783247b0e6a87</id><updated>2026-11-03T21:52:29Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T16:36:07Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261103-brazil-keeps-a-close-eye-on-us-midterm-elections" /><summary type="html">Brazil is keeping a close eye on the US midterm elections. Since Donald Trump's return to the White House, relations between Brasilia and Washington have grown increasingly tense. On the economic front, aggressive trade policies have subjected Brazilian imports to some of the steepest tariffs globally, exacerbating friction with the Trump administration. FRANCE 24's correspondent in Rio de Janeiro Jan Onoszko has more.</summary></entry><entry><title>‘Vile terrorist attack’: Russia bombs Ukraine aid centre</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7342bc856f2fe615ae0be67d8b1e368b434f9febf985648e97ee69c30ebba3a6</id><updated>2026-11-03T21:52:29Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T16:30:08Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261103-vile-terrorist-attack-russia-bombs-ukraine-aid-centre" /><summary type="html">A Russian “double tap” strike on a Ukrainian school being used as an aid distribution has killed at least 31 people, according to local authorities, with Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky dubbing it a “vile terrorist attack”.</summary></entry><entry><title>Trump focused on 'what's important to him': 'Tone-deaf for a normally shrewd populist operator'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b2ce074ef7df18f152ab96b364e8fbd7c92bba1f1f4ca08a3dc29b214cbbe6c2</id><updated>2026-11-03T21:52:29Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T16:05:32Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/trump-focused-on-what-s-important-to-him-tone-deaf-for-a-normally-shrewd-populist-operator--19609ba997e2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/trump-focused-on-what-s-important-to-him-tone-deaf-for-a-normally-shrewd-populist-operator" /><summary type="html">Erin Ogunkeye is pleased to welcome Doug Heye, Republican strategist, founder of Douglas Media, and former Communications Director for the Republican National Committee (RNC). As Americans head to the polls, Republicans face a challenge that goes beyond the familiar electoral backlash against an incumbent president. For Heye, Donald Trump's greatest political vulnerability may lie in the widening gap between his rhetoric of economic success and voters' everyday financial anxieties. "For a lot of voters, they see him focused on what's important to him, not what's important to them," Heye explains. Yet he also cautions against interpreting Democratic gains as a sign of renewed confidence in the opposition. Rather than a resurgence of partisan enthusiasm, the elections may expose an electorate increasingly disillusioned with both parties.</summary></entry><entry><title>Trump cuts Israeli military aid: $3.8 billion in security assistance slashed</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6d0caa37ea8176003a4548fd476be2dbece7acb40b0e223afde7c6e1f7eaaf89</id><updated>2026-11-03T21:52:29Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T16:01:30Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261103-trump-cuts-israeli-military-aid-3-8-billion-in-security-assistance-slashed--9e8be08da6ac.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261103-trump-cuts-israeli-military-aid-3-8-billion-in-security-assistance-slashed" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump on Tuesday, November 3, said he made a deal with Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu for Washington to stop providing $3.8 billion in funding to Israel after the end of this year. FRANCE 24's Jerusalem correspondent, Noga Tarnopolsky, has more.</summary></entry><entry><title>US midterms: Michigan Senate candidate El-Sayed becomes Democrats' rising star</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:25ac1b87ac97769c8536cceed7e4df5c67679efccd00c3f214723c5c0d5a9731</id><updated>2026-11-03T21:52:29Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T15:41:59Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261103-us-midterms-michigan-senate-candidate-el-sayed-becomes-democrats-rising-star--b86026836402.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261103-us-midterms-michigan-senate-candidate-el-sayed-becomes-democrats-rising-star" /><summary type="html">In the US midterm elections, Democrat Abdul El-Sayed and Republican Mike Rogers are testing two sharply different strategies to win over voters in one of the nation's premier swing states on Tuesday, November 3, in a closely watched race that could determine control of the Senate. Progressive candidate El-Sayed has so far outpolled his Republican rival and is emerging as one of the Democratic Party's rising stars.</summary></entry><entry><title>Bomb threats against European airlines force Warsaw airport closure, affect several flights</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:acc64da95aeabff5a49706effded75c9826cb2b58b7ac038c5340683632cc0f0</id><updated>2026-11-03T21:52:29Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T15:41:48Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261103-bomb-threats-disrupt-europe-flights" /><summary type="html">Bomb threats targeted at least 10 European airlines on Tuesday, forcing the temporary closure of a Warsaw airport and affecting at least four Ryanair flights. No explosives were found after the planes all took off and landed safely in different European cities.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>US midterms: Michigan candidate El-Sayed pledges to tackle the affordability crisis</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:81f7c1d04a3d86058fad4e36781d05d4bb19b5789c348e618591f8340900d1b4</id><updated>2026-11-03T21:52:29Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T15:34:27Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261103-us-midterms-michigan-candidate-el-sayed-pledges-to-tackle-the-affordability-crisis--9ec59f3a2e71.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261103-us-midterms-michigan-candidate-el-sayed-pledges-to-tackle-the-affordability-crisis" /><summary type="html">The cost of living is one of the main concerns for many US voters as the midterm elections get underway. In Michigan, Democratic Senate candidate Abdul El-Sayed has pledged to "take the money out of politics and put it in your pocket", as FRANCE 24 correspondent Jessica Le Masurier reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>A cultural stroll through Paris with actors François-Xavier Demaison and François Morel</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e2fc4d44999fa581ceb749bb17fac93e788287ef18ceed03f9c275f7d72b1df8</id><updated>2026-11-03T21:52:29Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T15:30:06Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/paris-des-arts/20261103-a-cultural-stroll-through-paris-with-actors-fran_ois-xavier-demaison-and-fran_ois-morel--6a2d65016129.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/paris-des-arts/20261103-a-cultural-stroll-through-paris-with-actors-fran%C3%A7ois-xavier-demaison-and-fran%C3%A7ois-morel" /><summary type="html">This week, we bring you a special programme dedicated to theatre. Valérie Fayolle takes us to the Renaissance Theatre, where François-Xavier Demaison takes us behind the scenes of "Laponie". The fiesty comedy shows how a family's holiday gathering can quickly turn into a settling of scores. "Theatre is one of our last collective experiences. It's magnificent, we're in a bubble," he tells us.</summary><category term="Paris des arts" /></entry><entry><title>King Charles says he has greater understanding of 'horrors' of slavery, falls short of apology</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:729e39540b3784725d4e1a9d728d845ed4b0bdb82d93bf35cc3fd43534a8c88a</id><updated>2026-11-03T21:52:29Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T15:26:37Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261103-king-charles-says-he-has-greater-understanding-of-horrors-of-slavery-falls-short-of-apology--ae418e66f435.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261103-king-charles-says-he-has-greater-understanding-of-horrors-of-slavery-falls-short-of-apology" /><summary type="html">King Charles III told the heads of 56 Commonwealth countries on Tuesday that he has a greater understanding of the horrors of slavery, calling it a "shameful chapter of history". This comes as Prime Minister Andy Burnham said he was open to the United Kingdom apologising for the transatlantic slave trade.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>'Your donut, your vote': Texas group uses free food to attract young voters</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:879b73919139c5b2ff09a0f5df5806cdccd5bc402cc0b2a7e8b7bb63a46c1c40</id><updated>2026-11-03T21:52:29Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T15:26:30Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261103-your-donut-your-vote-texas-group-uses-free-food-to-attract-young-voters--cd3ced7b6ae1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261103-your-donut-your-vote-texas-group-uses-free-food-to-attract-young-voters" /><summary type="html">US voters on Tuesday headed to the polls in midterm elections that could shape the political future of the country. But navigating the voting process can sometimes discourage voters – particularly younger ones. In Texas, an organisation reached out to them directly by handing out free food, to then help them overcome these obstacles. FRANCE 24's Special envoy Tarek Kai reports from Austin.</summary></entry><entry><title>Political parallels in France and the US: Anger at the ballot box and in the streets</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1c99a013b920bfdd0dac5c7326899e3b24227172c5455fbf6c404dd7a335c4c5</id><updated>2026-11-03T21:52:29Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T15:21:19Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/entre-nous/20261103-political-parallels-in-france-and-us-anger-at-the-ballot-box-and-in-the-streets--cb3c566a3efc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/entre-nous/20261103-political-parallels-in-france-and-us-anger-at-the-ballot-box-and-in-the-streets" /><summary type="html">Anger has long been a driving force for political change, but with the midterm elections in the US and the ongoing protests in France, widespread anger in both nations is currently front and centre. We take a look at some of the common issues causing this anger on both sides of the Atlantic, including the rising cost of living, a loss of faith in institutions and an eroding of the social contract.</summary><category term="Entre Nous" /></entry><entry><title>US midterms: All eyes on crucial Michigan Senate race</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:86dc5d32e0a2cb71f39209151a31a5b8ee454e9d9548bf0ba791fd2959e92b4e</id><updated>2026-11-03T21:52:29Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T15:15:48Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261103-us-midterms-all-eyes-on-crucial-michigan-senate-race--7781aa8be6b8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261103-us-midterms-all-eyes-on-crucial-michigan-senate-race" /><summary type="html">In the US midterm elections, the Senate race in Michigan has been one of the most closely watched in the country. It took an unexpected turn on Sunday after Democratic Congresswoman Haley Stevens endorsed Republican Mike Rogers over Democratic nominee Abdul El-Sayed. Both candidates made their final pitches to voters during campaign rallies on Monday evening, November 2. FRANCE 24's Jessica Le Masurier reports.</summary></entry></feed>
